TEST 13549 -- QoS: switchport interface - defaults to strict priority queueing
===========================================================================
Run:    2026-09-24 ~15:55-16:10 NZST, tb470
Build:  awplus_main-20260923-20
DUT:    IE520 3-member VCStack "IE520-stk"
        (Replaces the 2026-09-22 UNMEASURED "requires congestion this bench cannot create".
        The bench now has two host NICs that can drive ingress, and tb470 has tcpreplay,
        which sends ~983 Mbps per NIC.)

VERDICT: PASS -- the default scheduler is strict priority: 100% of the higher queue is
         transmitted, and the lower queue gets only what is left. This holds in both
         directions, so it follows the queue, not the port.

TOPOLOGY (temporary, reverted -- see teardown)
  Two ingress streams, each ~983 Mbps (tcpreplay --topspeed, 1518-byte tagged frames,
  10 s, simultaneous), converge on ONE 1G egress:
      ingress A  tb470 eth3 -> port3.0.9 (member 3), trunk, vlan 50 tagged
      ingress B  tb470 eth2 -> IE520-sa port1.0.2 (trunk, vlan 50) -> sa3 (trunk, vlan 50)
                 -> enters the stack on members 1/4
      egress     port3.0.13 (member 3), access vlan 50 -> tb470 eth1
  Queue selection = the 802.1p PCP in the tag ("Ingress traffic should be tagged").
  Received counts: tcpdump on eth1, one per source MAC, all with "0 packets dropped by
  kernel". Cross-checked against the DUT's egress queue counters on port3.0.13.
  eth1 sends a 1 pps learn frame so its MAC stays known in vlan 50.

STEP -- "Default config: sho mls qos int portx.x.x"
  mls qos enable (y/n prompt: y); no scheduling config applied.
  show mls qos interface port3.0.13: "Scheduler-set: None", 8 egress queues, each
    Status Enabled, Queue Limit 12%, Egress Rate Limit 0 Kb; Trust Mode: Ports default priority
  (No scheduler-set = the strict-priority default. The per-queue text does not print the
  word "strict"; the behaviour below is the evidence.)
  show mls qos maps cos-queue:  COS 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 -> QUEUE 2 0 1 3 4 5 6 7

TRAFFIC -- "100% of traffic from higher queue number should always be transmitted. Only
           buffered packets for lower queue should be transmitted."
  run                                  eth3 (A) rx/sent       eth2 (B) rx/sent       queues (port3.0.13)
  R0 both PCP 0 (same queue)           380936/819501  46.5%   443252/817501  54.2%   both Q2
  RA A=PCP5 (Q5), B=PCP2 (Q1)          819501/819501 100.0%     4660/817001   0.6%   Q5 tx 819501; Q1 drop 812341
  RB A=PCP2 (Q1), B=PCP5 (Q5)            8025/818001   1.0%   815501/815501 100.0%   Q5 tx 815501; Q1 drop 809976
  RC A=PCP2 top, B=PCP5 at 600 Mbps    323762/820501  39.5%   500000/500000 100.0%   Q5 tx 500000; Q1 tx 323762
  - The higher queue is delivered 100% in every run, whichever port and member it enters on
    (RA vs RB).
  - The lower queue gets only the leftover: ~0.6-1% against a line-rate higher queue, and
    ~384 Mbps (1G - 600M) in RC.
  - With both streams in the same queue (R0), the egress shares roughly evenly.

NOTES -- queue assignment for UNTAGGED traffic (a separate observation, not graded here;
         CAMPAIGN-QUEUE I-17)
  A first attempt used untagged frames, with the ingress CoS set per port, which is this
  case's sister 13553's method. Egress queue counters on port3.0.13 showed:
  - Untagged traffic entering on member 3 (port3.0.9) went to Q2 (CoS 0 -> Q2, per the map).
  - The same untagged traffic entering on members 1/4 (via sa3) went to Q0, with QoS off and
    with QoS on. Under strict priority that local stream beat it every time (e.g. 820501/820501
    vs 2672/822501).
  - `mls qos cos 5` on port3.0.9 was accepted (`show mls qos interface port3.0.9`: "Default
    CoS: 5"), but that port's untagged traffic stayed in Q2 instead of moving to Q5.
  Tagged traffic follows the map from either member (above), which is why the case's own
  "tagged" setup was used for the verdict.

TEARDOWN
  no mls qos (y/n: y); ports and sa3 back to access; vlan 50 removed on both units.
  Stack and IE520-sa running-configs diff IDENTICAL against their pre-test copies;
  show mls qos: Disable. Host paths eth1/eth2/eth3: 0% loss.
